# Line-ending policy (#45).
#
# The CI contract for this repo is a BYTE-FOR-BYTE diff: examples/contoso/verify.sh rebuilds the
# worked sample and diffs it against the committed fixtures. The renderers write via
# Path.write_text (engine/epac_builder/writeutil.py), so the *generated* bytes carry the build
# host's native newline — CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux/CI. That only works because what git
# STORES is normalized to LF; without this file it depended on each contributor's local
# core.autocrlf, and a checkout with autocrlf=false would commit CRLF fixtures and fail the
# ubuntu-latest byte-diff for a reason unrelated to any real change.
#
# Note this is only about the git-stored form. The catalogue's contentHash is already immune:
# engine/shared/hashing.py newline-normalizes before hashing (#27, slice 27e).

# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository, whatever the working tree looks like.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed by bash in CI and locally — CRLF here breaks the shebang line.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary: never normalize, never diff as text.
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
